--- body ---
## Context

This ticket owns one trait: **source-grounding of the master table** --
does each cell trace to its cited source? The verification method is
tier-1 deterministic string-match (fuzzy filename + plant-name lookup
against the 18-file RAG corpus). No LLM calls, no HITL.

Phase 1 code and results shipped in PR #261 (commit 13d53d5, 2026-04-16).
Slides carry the headline numbers (98% grounded, 80% traceable median,
0% for non-sourced baseline). All tests pass.

Two housekeeping items remain before close:

1. `report/inputs/generated/tab_source_grounding.tex` exists on disk
   (generated by `tabulate_source_grounding.py`) but is **untracked** --
   commit it.
2. No `\input` wires the table into `report.tex` -- add one in the
   appropriate verification-results section (Ch. 5 or Ch. 6).

## Scope boundary -- where Phases 2+3 went

The former Phases 2 (LLM adjudication) and 3 (HITL-ratified memory) are
**verification machinery**, not a trait of the table. Per the project
rule "one ticket = one trait x one target", they do not belong here.

- Tier-2/3 machinery belongs with the v0 fusion prototype (ticket 0076)
  and the escalation-rate trait ticket (0102, which already depends on
  that machinery). A separate reframing pass should add the Phase 2+3
  content to those tickets' bodies.
- Once that move is done, tickets 0098 and 0099 should block on
  0076/0102 rather than on 0097 full close.

## Exit criteria

- [x] `verify_source_grounding()` with tests (PR #261).
- [x] 2x2 table for 3 Opus sourced runs + non-sourced baseline.
- [x] Slides updated with automated grounding numbers.
- [ ] `tab_source_grounding.tex` committed to git.
- [ ] Table wired into report via `\input`.
